00:15:01,540 --> 00:15:02,923
Now!

270
00:15:02,923 --> 00:15:04,620
Finish it, Barou!

271
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:05,676
Got it.

272
00:15:07,580 --> 00:15:10,080
I've been played! Actually, it was Barou who would steal that ball!

273
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:12,080
Isagi used himself as bait

274
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:14,935
to create an opportunity for Barou to steal the ball!

275
00:15:14,935 --> 00:15:16,410
No, stop quickly!

276
00:15:16,410 --> 00:15:18,438
Go! Pass him, then score!

277
00:15:18,438 --> 00:15:20,816
Move aside, Muscle Obstacle Guy!

278
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:23,402
Fake chop move?

279
00:15:23,402 --> 00:15:26,446
This is the way to maximize Barou's uniqueness!

280
00:15:26,446 --> 00:15:28,200
Don't expect to pass me!

281
00:15:29,533 --> 00:15:31,160
Rin?

282
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:32,830
Rin!

283
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:37,833
Ball out of line, White Team throw-in.

284
00:15:37,833 --> 00:15:39,418
Damn!

285
00:15:39,418 --> 00:15:42,120
No, he didn't predict it.

286
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:44,750
He was just trying to respond to the situation.

287
00:15:44,750 --> 00:15:46,690
Rin was already standing in a position that allowed him

288
00:15:46,690 --> 00:15:49,595
to respond to the uncontrollable Barou.

289
00:15:49,595 --> 00:15:50,929
Both me and Rin, if we take one wrong step,

290
00:15:50,929 --> 00:15:53,056
the opponent will manage to score.

291
00:15:53,056 --> 00:15:56,410
To prevent this, we try to predict each other's movements.

292
00:15:56,410 --> 00:15:57,880
However, for Rin, Barou is

293
00:15:57,880 --> 00:15:59,950
an unpredictable player.

294
00:15:59,950 --> 00:16:01,648
Let's see, me who can maximize Barou's uniqueness

295
00:16:01,648 --> 00:16:04,109
or Rin who can minimize Barou's destructive power!

296
00:16:04,109 --> 00:16:07,080
The person who can control Barou and this entire field

297
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:09,323
will be the one to win this match.

298
00:16:12,284 --> 00:16:14,290
Amazing!

299
00:16:14,290 --> 00:16:16,360
At a very high standard,

300
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:18,700
they read each other's movements very intensely.

301
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:22,000
Now on this field...

302
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,120
there are two 'monsters'!

303
00:16:25,922 --> 00:16:28,500
The soccer game I long for...

304
00:16:29,580 --> 00:16:31,887
is right before my eyes!

305
00:16:32,580 --> 00:16:35,500
Finally, my dream of playing soccer with monsters...

306
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:38,894
is about to come true!

307
00:16:42,105 --> 00:16:43,421
Huh?

308
00:16:44,132 --> 00:16:45,587
What?

309
00:16:45,588 --> 00:16:48,987
Why? Even though I'm here.

310
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:53,200
I tried so hard not to be alone anymore.

311
00:16:55,250 --> 00:16:56,870
Yet, in the world of those two,

312
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,831
I don't exist.

313
00:17:00,791 --> 00:17:02,540
Why?

314
00:17:02,540 --> 00:17:06,619
They play soccer without me.

315
00:17:06,619 --> 00:17:08,450
Don't leave me!

316
00:17:08,450 --> 00:17:12,000
To me, you are 'monsters'.

317
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:15,430
But to you, what am I?

318
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:20,410
The one being tested is me.

319
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:26,858
Ball out, Red Team ball. Game restarts.

320
00:17:26,858 --> 00:17:28,660
Good, Chigiri!

321
00:17:28,660 --> 00:17:31,989
Sorry, I originally intended to pass to you.

322
00:17:31,989 --> 00:17:34,620
No, I'm the one who should apologize to you.

323
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:37,452
If we were faster, we could have stolen the ball.

324
00:17:37,452 --> 00:17:40,450
You're okay, right?

325
00:17:40,450 --> 00:17:41,957
Is your knee...

326
00:17:41,957 --> 00:17:44,910
No, my stamina is lacking.

327
00:17:44,910 --> 00:17:47,950
Don't worry about me.

328
00:17:47,950 --> 00:17:49,881
If you dare lose to Rin, I'll kill you.

329
00:17:49,881 --> 00:17:53,250
Okay. Then you also have to run

330
00:17:53,250 --> 00:17:54,845
until death.

331
00:17:54,845 --> 00:17:57,973
You don't need to tell me. I've been aware from the start!

332
00:17:58,620 --> 00:18:01,660
I can compete with Rin

333
00:18:01,660 --> 00:18:03,910
because Chigiri helps me intercept him.

334
00:18:03,910 --> 00:18:07,700
But it's impossible for him to keep moving at this speed.

335
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:10,620
More precisely, not just Chigiri,

336
00:18:10,620 --> 00:18:12,330
all players including me,

337
00:18:12,330 --> 00:18:15,120
our stamina is draining quickly.

338
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:17,750
Everyone is maintaining a very high performance.

339
00:18:17,750 --> 00:18:19,290
If the condition drops a little now,

340
00:18:19,290 --> 00:18:22,664
it will immediately affect the quality of passes and movement.

341
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:26,330
The person who masters this small change

342
00:18:26,330 --> 00:18:28,295
will be able to control the final outcome of the match.

343
00:18:30,422 --> 00:18:32,660
Rin, I'm returning it to you.

344
00:18:33,133 --> 00:18:35,000
To me again?

345
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,750
What kind of attack style is this?

346
00:18:36,750 --> 00:18:40,500
Damn, they keep pushing forward.

347
00:18:41,330 --> 00:18:43,060
This is a strategy that hasn't been used until now.

348
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:45,840
Keep kicking the ball before Chigiri steals it

349
00:18:45,840 --> 00:18:47,399
and I'll make the decision.

350
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:51,580
But there's nothing unique about Rin's passes.

351
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:53,580
No, that's not it!

352
00:18:53,580 --> 00:18:57,000
The only person who can do a center breakthrough is

353
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:59,117
- the one who stays strong until the end.
- Stop!

354
00:18:59,117 --> 00:19:01,703
- Responding to Rin's passes and continuing to run.
- Barou, quickly block him!

355
00:19:01,703 --> 00:19:05,957
Muscle Monster, the person with unlimited stamina!

356
00:19:05,957 --> 00:19:09,419
Tokimitsu, turns out he's not just all muscle.

357
00:19:09,419 --> 00:19:10,870
He's coming.

358
00:19:10,870 --> 00:19:13,256
Pass in front of the goal.

359
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:15,910
Don't hope!

360
00:19:15,910 --> 00:19:16,927
Wait a moment!

361
00:19:18,330 --> 00:19:22,410
Catching from behind and an intentional tackle.

362
00:19:22,410 --> 00:19:24,750
Shouei Barou and Hyoma Chigiri, both players are given

363
00:19:24,750 --> 00:19:25,769
yellow cards as a warning.

364
00:19:26,580 --> 00:19:28,040
This was clearly a legal physical contact!

365
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:29,910
I only hit the ball!

366
00:19:29,910 --> 00:19:32,067
Can you see clearly? Bad VAR!

367
00:19:32,067 --> 00:19:36,405
Rin, sorry, I only got a free kick.

368
00:19:36,405 --> 00:19:40,290
Damn, the chemical reaction between Tokimitsu and Rin.

369
00:19:40,290 --> 00:19:42,650
If I could guess faster than Rin,

370
00:19:42,650 --> 00:19:44,371
I could have prevented it from the start.

371
00:19:44,371 --> 00:19:47,833
But we both haven't conceded a goal yet.

372
00:19:47,833 --> 00:19:51,586
This free kick, don't hope it will succeed.

373
00:19:51,586 --> 00:19:55,120
This distance is very dangerous.

374
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:57,290
It's completely within Rin's shooting range.

375
00:19:57,290 --> 00:19:59,120
A little more this way.

376
00:19:59,120 --> 00:20:01,080
Two people forming a wall?

377
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:02,889
Will he shoot directly

378
00:20:02,889 --> 00:20:05,200
or pass?

379
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:07,602
Rin has these two options.

380
00:20:07,602 --> 00:20:10,580
Meanwhile, if he shoots, I'll be part of the wall.

381
00:20:10,580 --> 00:20:13,567
If he passes, I'll steal the ball in an area with few people.

382
00:20:13,567 --> 00:20:16,870
But if I jump, I won't have time to steal the ball.

383
00:20:16,870 --> 00:20:19,072
So I have to respond when he lifts his leg.

384
00:20:20,031 --> 00:20:23,201
Will he shoot or pass? Which one?

385
00:20:26,910 --> 00:20:30,208
A vertical spin ball that flew past my head and fell behind!

386
00:20:32,660 --> 00:20:34,200
I was tricked!

387
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:36,580
He didn't give me any time to respond,

388
00:20:36,580 --> 00:20:40,510
a high-speed free kick that went right past my head.

389
00:20:40,510 --> 00:20:43,330
You hesitated whether I would shoot or pass, right?

390
00:20:43,330 --> 00:20:44,973
What an absurd analysis method.

391
00:20:44,973 --> 00:20:48,435
In a situation like this, how could you choose just one?

392
00:20:48,435 --> 00:20:50,080
"I'm the one who shoots and scores."

393
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:52,397
There's only this one answer from the start.

394
00:20:53,370 --> 00:20:54,540
Is that so.

395
00:20:54,540 --> 00:20:56,040
Both Rin and Isagi,

396
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:58,390
they always play so that they can shoot themselves

397
00:20:58,390 --> 00:21:01,660
and for the sake of individualism.

398
00:21:01,660 --> 00:21:03,450
Meanwhile,

399
00:21:04,750 --> 00:21:07,450
what do I play soccer for?

400
00:21:08,700 --> 00:21:11,870
For finding the true 'monster'?

401
00:21:11,870 --> 00:21:14,085
Because I want to have a friend?

402
00:21:15,370 --> 00:21:16,830
I can't.

403
00:21:16,830 --> 00:21:18,980
With reasons like this,

404
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:21,551
how could I possibly catch up to them?

405
00:21:23,370 --> 00:21:25,330
What is the meaning of

406
00:21:25,330 --> 00:21:26,790
my individualism?

407
00:21:29,250 --> 00:21:33,063
(Episode 21: Without Me)

408
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,990
Blue Lock Extra Scene!

409
00:23:06,990 --> 00:23:07,750
(#21 The Other Three-Person Team, Part Two)

410
00:23:07,750 --> 00:23:10,630
We must choose team members wisely.

411
00:23:10,630 --> 00:23:11,410
(Ikki Niko)

412
00:23:11,410 --> 00:23:14,150
Choosing team members who don't have skills that I have

413
00:23:14,150 --> 00:23:16,160
is the best decision.

414
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:19,370
A useful person.

415
00:23:20,080 --> 00:23:20,570
(Zantetsu Tsurugi)

416
00:23:20,570 --> 00:23:23,080
He is a very fast person, but his thinking ability is very poor.

417
00:23:24,090 --> 00:23:27,700
Zantetsu, have you decided who to form a team with?

418
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:31,473
I'm waiting for Nagi and Reo.

419
00:23:31,473 --> 00:23:33,830
Maybe this person will do.

420
00:23:33,830 --> 00:23:37,479
The two of them might already be in the next stage.

421
00:23:39,080 --> 00:23:41,410
So there was a possibility like that.

422
00:23:41,410 --> 00:23:44,620
It can't be helped, we just have to start from scratch.

423
00:23:44,620 --> 00:23:47,697
He must not have expected a situation like this.

424
00:23:47,697 --> 00:23:50,325
Then, want to form a team with me?

425
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:54,830
If I form a team with you, what's the "loss" for me?

426
00:23:54,830 --> 00:23:56,080
Do you mean "benefit"?

427
00:23:56,080 --> 00:23:57,540
Yes.

428
00:23:57,540 --> 00:24:01,127
I know best how to use your talent compared to others.

429
00:24:01,127 --> 00:24:02,120
(Bangs Person)

430
00:24:02,120 --> 00:24:03,080
(Giving Instructions)

431
00:24:03,080 --> 00:24:05,040
(I Am Very Active)

432
00:24:05,040 --> 00:24:07,550
(Doing Missions) Go, Zantetsu!

433
00:24:07,550 --> 00:24:10,910
(The Definitely Winning Footballer) I am someone who never fails.

434
00:24:11,388 --> 00:24:13,973
No one knows I'm stupid, great!

435
00:24:13,973 --> 00:24:18,200
Alright, there's a saying, "Yesterday's friend is today's friend."

436
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:20,540
The correct one is "yesterday's enemy."

437
00:24:20,540 --> 00:24:22,941
He's really stupid.

438
00:24:22,941 --> 00:24:26,080
Then, who do you want to choose for the remaining one person?

439
00:24:26,080 --> 00:24:28,000
The remaining one person...

440
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:28,760
(Zantetsu, Niko, Form a Team)

441
00:24:28,760 --> 00:24:31,830
Just find someone who can communicate smoothly.